hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24043","Narrated to us Abd al-Rahman, from Sufyan, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from a man of Banu Damrah, from a man of his people, he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Aqiqah, and he said: I do not like disobedience, but whoever has a child born to him and wishes to sacrifice for him, let him do so."
"24044","Narrated to us Sufyan ibn Uyaynah, narrated to us Zayd ibn Aslam, from a man, from his father or from his uncle, that he said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Arafah, and he was asked about the Aqiqah, and he said: I do not like disobedience, but whoever has a child born to him and wishes to sacrifice for him, let him do so."
